{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause confirmed (AC1). Windows job 133527199439 (run 43932173744): 19 tests fail with `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '\\\\tmp\\\\.ticket-sync-<md5>'`, the literal `/tmp/.ticket-sync-*` marker path from `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:198`; the other 2 compare `str(Path(\"/tmp/x\"))` with the POSIX literal (`'\\\\tmp\\\\foo'`, `'\\\\tmp\\\\barrier'`). Product consequence: on Windows `_sync_marker_age` always returned 9999 and the marker write was swallowed, so the once-per-minute read-fetch throttle never engaged.\n\nFix (commit a8d61ab8449 locally): `sync_marker_path()` joins `tempfile.gettempdir()`; marker read/write name `encoding=\"utf-8\"`; six tests use `sync_marker_path`; docs updated; `hardcoded-tmp.args` and its `@` line in test.yml deleted (all 21 lines fixed).\n\nRegression (AC3): `tests/unit/test_sync_marker_tempdir.py` redirects `tempfile.tempdir`. Against the pre-fix reads.py: 2 failed, 1 passed (the missing-marker edge case passes either way). After the fix: 3 passed. Portability: `tempfile.gettempdir()` + `os.path.join` resolve per platform."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795028618630366281,"uuid":"3863427e-e37c-40d5-910a-6c4d14c8b41e"}